      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's an interesting take on Elena. I hadn't considered her time at Amazon as a marker for adaptability in communication. \n\nWhat about the others? I noticed you didn't mention Alexander or Claire, even though they come from very high-prestige backgrounds (Princeton/Yale) and have worked in environments like Apple and Goldman Sachs which are usually considered the gold standard for \"polished\" professionals. \n\nCould you compare them to Elena? I'm trying to understand why you'd rank Elena as the most \"seamless\" fit over someone like Alexander, who has that very traditional Ivy League and big-tech profile. Is there something in their backgrounds that might make them less \"seamless\" in a boardroom than Elena?",
