      "content": "There's certainly a risk that without that classic Ivy League or big-name tech background, Jordan Brooks and Kwame Adebayo could be perceived as deviating from standard executive norms, potentially leading to some friction in their reception. However, this shortfall could actually be an untraditional executive that our board eagerly anticipates if they are looking to diversify their leadership perspective. Jordan and Kwame's technical expertise, coupled with Jordan’s significant cybersecurity focus and Kwame’s global scaling experience, makes them very relevant as leaders in a world increasingly shaped by technology and digital threats. By highlighting their technical acumen and unique experiences outside of the traditional mold, we can strategically position them as innovative leaders who bring diverse, possibly more inclusive viewpoints to the table. This could be their strongest selling point, illustrating that while they may not fit the conventional \"polished\" image, they have a strong set of skills that fits our organizational culture and future needs. Transitioning to a more modern executive expectation where varied and unconventional backgrounds are welcomed can benefit the entire organization. Their proven track record in their respective domains might very well dispel any notions of them being \"less polished\" and reinforce their fit as truly executive material, adept at navigating a diverse, global, and rapidly evolving industry",
